{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>So that your days and the days of your children may multiply upon the land.</b> In tractate Berakhot (8a) they said to Rabbi Yohanan: Are there old men in Babylonia? He was astonished, for is it not written: ״לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ יְמֵיכֶם וִימֵי בְנֵיכֶם עַל הָאֲדָמָה״ — which implies, but outside the Land, no. They said to him: They come early and stay late at the synagogue. He said: That is what benefits them. And the difficulty with this answer is that the question still stands in its place, for in this verse it says simply ״עַל הָאֲדָמָה״ without any distinction, and whence does he learn to say that this verse speaks specifically of a time when they are not going to the synagogue, to say that only then are days curtailed?" "And it appears to me along the lines of what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Megillah 29a) that in the future the synagogues and study halls of outside the Land are destined to be established fixedly in the Land of Israel, etc. — and if so, the earth of all the synagogues of outside the Land is itself the earth of the Land of Israel, for in the future HaShem will establish the synagogues — structure and ground, entirely — in the Land of Israel; and if so, that earth is certainly holy earth and a portion of the earth of the Land of Israel. And one who rises early and stays late every day at the synagogues is as though every day he stands upon the earth that HaShem swore to the Fathers, and the promise ״לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ יְמֵיכֶם וִימֵי בְנֵיכֶם עַל הָאֲדָמָה אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע ה׳ לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶם לָתֵת לָהֶם״ is fulfilled in him — ״to you״ is not said, but ״to them,״ Rashi explained; from here is a proof for the resurrection of the dead from the Torah. And what does this matter have to do with here? Rather, because specifically at that time the synagogues of outside the Land will be established in the Land of Israel. And it could be that this refers back to the beginning of the parashah, where it says: ״וּלְעָבְדוֹ בְכָל לְבַבְכֶם״ — this is prayer, as Rashi explained; and since it says ״בְכָל לְבַבְכֶם״ (with all your heart), infer from it that it speaks of many people gathering at the synagogues to pray, and concerning this HaShem promised the reward: ״לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ יְמֵיכֶם וִימֵי בְנֵיכֶם עַל הָאֲדָמָה״." "And as for why the matter was made dependent specifically on coming early and staying late, you will find it well explained in our work Oholot Ephraim, in the Gate of Prayer, discourse 503, along the lines of the verse ״לִשְׁקֹד עַל דַּלְתוֹתַי יוֹם יוֹם לִשְׁמֹר מְזוּזוֹת פְּתָחָי״ (Proverbs 8:34), ״לְשִׁכְנוֹ תִדְרְשׁוּ וּבָאתָ שָׁמָּה״, and you will find the whole matter explained well there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "The abbreviation תק״ג could resolve to 503; I have rendered it numerically. Oholot Ephraim (עלילות אפרים / עוללות אפרים) is the Kli Yakar's own earlier work. The verse citation from Proverbs 8:34 is given in the text without an explicit address."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:12:41.185123376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}